  "worked_solution": "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{h}^{\u2032}(t)\u2248\\frac{h(t)-h(t-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=3.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{\u2032}(3) & \u2248\\frac{h(3)-h(3-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{h(3)-h(2)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{159-181}{1} \\\\  & =-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the rate of change of the altitude is $-22\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}.$",
